// Satoshi Market storefront mark — neon market-stall icon with the Bitcoin
// glyph (orange disc + white B) centred inside the stall. v3.1.1: the original
// render sat on an OPAQUE near-black JPEG field; under mixBlendMode:"screen"
// that field "dropped out" only over a dark card, but over the amber off-route
// tint the screen-lift exposed the JPEG's rectangular bounding box as a hard
// square seam. Fixed by keying that dark navy field to TRUE ALPHA (transparent
// PNG): the field no longer paints, so the storefront renders cleanly over ANY
// backdrop (dark OR amber) with no square — and the approved screen-blend glow
// on dark tiles is preserved (a transparent field is identical to a crushed-to-
// black one under `screen` over a dark card). Keyed from the prior raster by
// alpha = f(navy-ness): dark AND cool (blue>red) -> transparent; warm/bright
// storefront -> opaque. Downscaled to 256px (renders at 128px). data-URL idiom.
export const STORE_WATERMARK =
  "data:image/png;base64,";
